{"name":"Folkstone","hex":"#6d6562","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Folkestone","blocks":[{"text":"Folkestone is a coastal town on the English Channel, in Kent, south-east England. The town lies on the southern edge of the North Downs at a valley between two cliffs. It was an important harbour, shipping port, and fashionable coastal resort for most of the 19th and mid-20th centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Folkestone_Harbour_with_Viaduct_and_Swing_Bridge.png/330px-Folkestone_Harbour_with_Viaduct_and_Swing_Bridge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folkestone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg/500px-The_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg/1280px-The_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg/500px-The_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Church_of_St_Mary_and_St_Eanswythe_at_Folkestone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4928349.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Guildhall_Street%2C_Folkestone_%28geograph_3828843%29.jpg/500px-Guildhall_Street%2C_Folkestone_%28geograph_3828843%29